        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): harden JSON.parse in secrets apply and model-auth status",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTwo unguarded `JSON.parse()` calls in the CLI can crash with raw `SyntaxError` exceptions instead of producing user-friendly errors or graceful fallbacks:\n\n1. **`src/cli/secrets-cli.ts:56`** — `readPlanFile()` calls `JSON.parse(raw)` on a plan file read from disk. A corrupt/malformed plan file throws a raw `SyntaxError` with stack trace instead of a friendly error message telling the user how to regenerate the plan.\n\n2. **`src/cli/capability-cli.ts:938`** — `runModelAuthStatus()` captures stdout from `modelsStatusCommand`, finds a line starting with `{`, and parses it. If the captured output contains a malformed JSON fragment, the `model-auth status` command crashes instead of gracefully returning `{}`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoth are minimal defensive wrappings:\n- `readPlanFile`: wrap in try/catch, throw a friendly `Error` with the file path and the regenerate command\n- `runModelAuthStatus`: wrap in try/catch, return `{}` as graceful degradation (caller already handles empty results)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real terminal output (7 assertions, real file I/O):\n```\n$ npx tsx _proof-harden-jsonparse.ts\n=== Proof: Hardened JSON.parse in CLI ===\n\nsecrets-cli readPlanFile (real file round-trip):\nPASS   Before fix: raw SyntaxError on corrupt file\nPASS   After fix: friendly Error with file path and malformed JSON guidance\nPASS   Valid plan file parses correctly (no regression)\n\ncapability-cli runModelAuthStatus (unparseable CLI output):\nPASS   Before fix: SyntaxError on unparseable output\nPASS   After fix: graceful {} when captured line is not valid JSON\nPASS   After fix: valid JSON still parses correctly (no regression)\nPASS   After fix: no JSON-like lines returns empty object\n\n=== Results: 7 passed, 0 failed ===\n```\n\n### Regression tests (in existing CLI test files):\n- `src/cli/secrets-cli.test.ts`: corrupt plan file → friendly error with \"malformed JSON\" and file path (no SyntaxError)\n- `src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts`: unparseable model auth status output → `{}` (no crash)\n\n## Merge Risk\n\nLow — defensive try/catch wrappers. Valid JSON paths are unchanged. No new dependencies, no logic changes.",
